  "name": "capture-answer-timeout",
  "description": "Change C18: a capture the host never answers resolves capture.answerTimeoutMs (here 2000) after it was requested (timer capture.answer.<requestId>) as paint_readiness_timeout with failure answer_timeout, and records a capture_diagnostic even without the captureDiagnostics capability, so hosts can count it. The queue then runs on. Here the host drops the route capture a navigation in the background asked for; the lifecycle capture of the resume waits behind it and is issued at the deadline. A late answer to the timed-out id is ignored and its frame released; later captures work normally. Dart has no answer deadline.",
